# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
# claude code
# Directory contents ignored by default; un-ignore the committed project
# config so it can be reviewed like CI config. settings.local.json is also
# gitignored globally via ~/.gitignore_global. Note the pattern is `.claude/*`
# (contents) not `.claude/` (directory) — git can't re-include children of an
# excluded directory.
#
# 2026-05-05 (ADR-0020 substrate session): re-included .claude/skills/ as
# load-bearing project infrastructure per CLAUDE.md ("Skills in
# .claude/skills/ summarize and point"). The `.claude/skills/` directory
# was silently gitignored from 2026-04-19 (skills migration) until the
# 2026-05-05 architecture-substrate session's pre-flight surfaced the gap.
# Both `!.claude/skills/` and `!.claude/skills/**` are required because
# git can't re-include children of an excluded directory without first
# re-including the directory itself plus its recursive contents.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

# playwright e2e — storageState cookies are credentials
tests/e2e/.auth/
# playwright reports / results
playwright-report/
test-results/

# runtime log capture — the historical `pnpm dev 2>&1 | tee "logs/..."` pattern
# was the direct cause of a Next.js watcher feedback storm (Session 8 C6-pre
# finding; the prereq doc at docs/07_governance/ec-2-prompt-set.md now points
# log capture at /tmp/ instead). /logs/ stays ignored as defense-in-depth in
# case the old pattern re-appears in a future prereq.
/logs/

# Session coordination — lock file is per-session, not tracked
.coordination/session-lock.json

# Working artifacts directory — verification reports, audit scratch, and
# other non-canonical outputs from docs / governance arcs. Canonical records
# live in docs/ proper. Pre-existing reports/mutation/ contents (mutation
# testing output) become gitignored by extension; their disposition is
# deferred to a separate cleanup arc. Round-2 docs reorganization
# (2026-05-07) is the precondition for this rule; see
# DOCS_RESTRUCTURE_V2.md Part 3 (Session 7) for the canonical record.
#
# Scope refined 2026-05-10 at chunk B5-3-D1 session #1 checkpoint #1 per
# founder verdict: pattern updated from `reports/` (matches at any depth)
# to `/reports/` (root-only) to align rule scope with documented intent.
# The bare-pattern form was silently capturing application source paths
# named `reports/` at deeper paths (e.g., `apps/web/src/services/spend/
# reports/` D1.3 substrate + the already-tracked `apps/web/src/app/api/
# orgs/[orgId]/reports/` API routes tree). Catch #23 + #24 logged for
# D1 closeout friction-journal forward-pointer.
/reports/
